<title>UK: Renold H1 pretax profit 10.2 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Renold H1 pretax profit 10.2 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.0		   vs  9.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  2.8		   vs  2.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.2		   vs  8.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   91.3		   vs 87.3</p>
<p> Trading profit	   10.5		   vs  8.6</p>
<p> Interest payable	  0.3		   vs  0.5</p>
<p> Tax			   2.7		   vs  1.7</p>
<p> Net taxed		   7.5		   vs  6.4</p>
<p> Retained profit	   5.6		   vs  4.7</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 24, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 26  Ex-div date		November 18</p>
<p>NOTE - UK engineering group Renold Plc said that its first half performance had shown the benefits of its wide geographical spread and range of markets served, &quot;as well as the attention given to production efficiency and cost management&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
